# k12: the wmma + cp.async double buffer. Same tile as k14, so the same
# per-iteration design point (4096 tensor flops, at most 64 global bytes
# via cp.async) and the same A100 machine line; the fragments come
# through wmma.load from shared (4 A x 16 B + 16 B x 16 B = 320 B), the
# kernel's totals' terms in K/16. Each CTA declares 16384 B of shared
# memory. The loop's guard `K + 15 > 30` tests its latch at k = 0,
# ⌊K/16⌋ > 0, so the loop is counted per execution of the guard: its
# tensor flops over the kernel, 4096·(K/16) per thread, are exact. The
# text report pins the loop ranking, the iteration's instruction tally,
# AI(global) >= 64, no unknowns and full coverage.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/k12/k12.sm_80.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/k12/k12.sm_80.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
CHECK: loop with the most instructions (static): 12_double_buffer.cuh:114
CHECK: loop 12_double_buffer.cuh:114 ($L__BB0_5)
CHECK: instructions = <= 98
CHECK: shared load 16 B                                        20
CHECK: {{  }}wmma.load.b.sync.aligned.row.m16n16k16.shared.f16     16
CHECK: {{  }}wmma.load.a.sync.aligned.row.m16n16k16.shared.f16      4
CHECK: tensor f16                                              16
CHECK: {{  }}wmma.mma.sync.aligned.row.row.m16n16k16.f32.f32       16
CHECK: AI(global) >= 64 flop/B
CHECK: unknowns: none
CHECK: coverage: instructions_classified 100.0%
CHECK: coverage: loop_trips_resolved 100.0% (1/1)
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry _Z19hgemm_double_bufferILi128ELi128ELi16ELi64ELi64ELi128EEviiifPK6__halfS2_fPS0_( // shared memory 16,384 B/CTA | per thread: flops f32 <= 384; tensor flops f16 (4096·(param_2 / 16)); global load <= (64·(param_2 / 16) + 384) B, store <= 512 B; shared load (320·(param_2 / 16)) B, store <= (64·(param_2 / 16) + 128) B; param load <= 48 B{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}$L__BB0_5: // loop: trips param_2 / 16 | under line 225 | exec (param_2 / 16)/thread{{$}}
